  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "the trance build: a snare roll that doubles its rate every few bars — quarters, eighths, sixteenths — over the kick, into the drop",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "Eight bars: two of quarters, two of eighths, four of sixteenths rising from quiet to full. It belongs in the build alone, and the pin cannot place it there: a track pin plays its cells in every drummed section, so the roll loops through the mains too. The riser that goes with it is scheduled by rules and a row can only want it. Both are in the gap list."
